ead adriana well exactly  that gail you know tell us about your  son and how you say that it's made you  stronger i mean i feel like motherhood  it just makes you a better version of  who you are right and my son nico is  absolutely the greatest so after he was  born we received a diagnosis of down  syndrome um he has down syndrome and  profound hearing loss so over the course  of his life he's overcome so many  challenges and fortunately for this  olympics i was able to donate my opening  ceremony jacket to the national down  syndrome society  and we raised 5 000 one dollars and one  of my partners bridgestone they believe  in family community all these types of  things they actually doubled the  donation so uh ten thousand and two  dollars so to speak they double the  donation to national down syndrome  society and i wanted to use my olympic  platform to really showcase him and  showcase all the people in the  disability community and how much work  they go through day in and day out to  have the greatest lives possible elana i  know it's still sinking in but what's  next  i have no idea  that's a good answer that's a great  answer  more medals yes more battles hopefully  we'll see where i go from an athletic  standpoint but definitely going to enjoy  being a mom for a little bit yeah enjoy  you deserve it thank you so much alana  myers taylor thank you

